   "content": "<p>… distance away he fell ill. In 158 AH, at the age of 63, after ruling for approximately twenty-two years, he departed from this transitory world.</p><p>Character and achievements:</p><p>Mansur faced internal and external dangers, but with his high abilities and intelligence he gained control over all the difficulties and dangers. Through his wise works he succeeded in bringing his boat out safe and sound. In Mansur&#x27;s era of government, where revolts ended, there the series of conquests too continued. In Mansur&#x27;s era the subjects were prosperous, and things of daily use were available at extremely cheap prices. Mansur strengthened the caliphate of the Banu Abbas with continuous and tireless labour; that is why he alone is called the real founder of the Banu Abbas. He was regular in fasting and prayer. He hated luxury and pleasure-seeking. He always wore simple and ordinary dress. Mansur was frugal of the highest degree. He was strongly against extravagance. In connection with rebels he used force. Ruler and ruled, master and slave, rich and poor — he did equal justice with all. Mansur&#x27;s routine was that he led the Fajr prayer himself. After that he performed his particular duties in the court. This series continued till afternoon. After the &#x27;Asr prayer he came home. After the &#x27;Isha prayer the letters of the walis and other officials were read; after taking the necessary action on them he would go to sleep. He had spread a network of spies in the sultanate, who kept him informed of the activities of the governors and walis. Necessary action was taken on their reports. One merit of Mansur was also that he remained steadfast even in extremely unfavourable circumstances and …</p>",
