   "content": "<p>They began to be treated with gentleness, love and sympathy.</p><p>Revolt of the zindiqs:</p><p>The meaning of zand is interpretation. They used to interpret the scriptures of other religions according to their own will; therefore they were called zindiq. In this very era Hakam bin Hakim, the katib of Abu Muslim Khurasani, claimed divinity. His belief was that Allah the Exalted had become incarnate in the body of Hazrat Adam (peace be upon him); in Adam (peace be upon him) and Nuh (peace be upon him), and in this way in the forms of all the prophets, Allah the Exalted kept being transferred; this series reached Abu Muslim; after Abu Muslim it has now been transferred into me. It is said that by jugglery he had brought out an artificial moon from a well near Nakhshab in Transoxiana, whose light spread far and wide. Hakam bin Hakim was very ugly. He usually went about wearing a veil; that is why he was called &quot;Muqanna&#x27;&quot; or &quot;Burqa&#x27;i&quot;. Through his sorcery he had gathered people around him. Mahdi sent Mu&#x27;adh bin Muslim and Sa&#x27;id Harashi against Muqanna&#x27;. Sa&#x27;id Harashi besieged Muqanna&#x27;. When Muqanna&#x27; saw no way of escape, he killed his family by giving them poison, lit a fire, and burnt himself in it along with all his companions. This was the end of the claimant of divinity!</p><p>Roman attacks and revolts:</p><p>The Romans had begun attacks on Islamic regions. Mahdi confronted them personally. Later he sent Harun off with an army of one hundred thousand. The Romans accepted obedience but the next year went back on their promise. Mahdi …</p>",
