   "content": "<p>Ma&#x27;mun al-Rashid</p><p>813 CE to 833 CE</p><p>Accession:</p><p>After the killing of his brother Amin, Ma&#x27;mun ascended the throne in Muharram 198 AH. Ma&#x27;mun&#x27;s upbringing had been done by Ja&#x27;far. He had heartfelt attachment to the sciences. The academic progress of his era is specially famous. Ma&#x27;mun had obtained the throne through the efforts of Fadl bin Sahl; therefore Ma&#x27;mun made him prime minister — indeed all the powers of the government were with him. Fadl wanted to remain in power forever. So he advised the caliph that instead of Baghdad, Merv itself be kept as the capital. He accepted the proposal, and from 813 CE to 819 CE Merv remained the capital. During this time in Baghdad …</p>",
