   "theory": "… made Ishaq bin Ibrahim his deputy and himself attacked Roman regions and conquered several of their important forts. When Ma'mun reached back in Syria, the Caesar of Rome caused havoc. In 217 AH Ma'mun attacked again and conquered the fort of Lu'lu'ah too.\n\nVizierate:\n\nMa'mun's first vizier was Fadl bin Sahl. Fadl was a great learned scholar and an expert politician. But, keeping Ma'mun unaware of conditions, Fadl himself kept dominating power. Ma'mun had him killed at the place of Sarakhs while bathing in a bath-house. After Fadl he appointed his brother Hasan bin Sahl vizier and with extreme pomp made a historic marriage with his beautiful daughter Buran. Hasan's mental balance became disturbed and he passed away in this very state. After Hasan, Ahmad was appointed vizier, but he died in 211 AH. He was a very good man. After Ahmad, Ibn Yusuf became vizier. Ibn Yusuf was a great learned scholar, but envious courtiers got him dismissed and beaten. He died of this very shock. Ma'mun's last vizier was Ibn Yazdad, who held his post until Ma'mun's death.\n\nDeath:\n\nIn 218 AH Ma'mun set out for the fourth time to attack the Romans, but on the way, at the place of Tarsus, after being ill for a few days he departed from this world.",
