   "content": "<p>Abu al-Abbas Ahmad bin Mutawakkil al-Mu&#x27;tamid &#x27;ala Allah</p><p>869 CE to 892 CE</p><p>Mu&#x27;tamid ascended the throne in 256 AH. His age was 25 years. He ruled for approximately 23 years, but the government was in reality in the hands of his brother Muwaffaq billah. Mu&#x27;tamid was a ruler in name only.</p><p>National disarray and disturbances:</p><p>When Mu&#x27;tamid ascended the throne, disturbances began in the country. The whole country had come into the grip of disarray and revolts. The Saffarids had taken possession of Sijistan, Kirman, Fars and Khurasan. The storm of Ibn Sufi (Egypt) was advancing like a hurricane. The Abbasid armies were failing. The power of the Abbasid government was declining. According to Suyuti, he took possession of Basrah and destroyed it, and swept away the settlements around it like straw. Ya&#x27;qub Saffar put an end to the Tahirid government. At last Saffar&#x27;s confrontation was with Mu&#x27;tamid. Mu&#x27;tamid was wounded and suffered defeat. He had become fed up with his helplessness, because all powers were with Muwaffaq. He tried to obtain refuge with the amir Ibn Tulun, because only he was strong enough to help the caliph. Mu&#x27;tamid set off for Egypt, but Muwaffaq had him returned from the way. Ibn Tulun confronted Muwaffaq but suffered defeat.</p><p>Death:</p><p>Mu&#x27;tamid died in Rajab 279 AH.</p>",
