     "text": "… life be breathed. He was a first-rate statesman and an awe-inspiring caliph, but unfortunately he could not obtain release from the Daylamis, and in his era too they remained dominant. In his era the Ghaznavid government made great progress. But according to the famous historian Firishtah, the relations of Mahmud Ghaznavi and al-Qadir billah were strained. In 380 AH Samsam al-Dawlah was killed. In 402 AH Baha' al-Dawlah passed away. His son Sultan al-Dawlah Abu al-Qasim ascended the throne. In 415 AH Sultan al-Dawlah died and in 416 AH Sharaf al-Dawlah passed away. After Sharaf al-Dawlah, Jalal al-Dawlah ascended the throne. In 421 AH Mahmud Ghaznavi passed away. In 421 AH al-Qadir fell seriously ill. He appointed his son Abdullah his heir-apparent. al-Qadir died in 422 AH.",
