   "theory": "… events the world of Islam was affected.\n\nIn North Africa the Murabitun rose as a power. They gave the Muslims of Spain deliverance from the oppressions of the Christian rulers. In the battle of Zallaqa they gave the Christians a historic defeat. Alfonso II was wounded. Yusuf bin Tashfin went back. But when wars began again among the Muslim rulers, he came back to Spain, ended all the Islamic governments and established a united government.\n\nThe most important event of Ahmad's era is the First Crusade, in which all Europe had surged against the Muslims. The Seljuqs tried with great bravery to stop this storm but could not succeed. Bayt al-Maqdis was earlier in the possession of the Seljuqs, but at that time the Fatimids of Egypt had taken possession of it. They could not save Bayt al-Maqdis from the onslaught of the Christians. The Christians, taking possession of Bayt al-Maqdis, inflicted such oppressions on the Muslims that humanity trembled.\n\nDeath:\n\nAhmad bin Muqtadi died in 512 AH. His age was 42 years. One year before his death, in 511 AH, the Seljuq ruler Sultan Muhammad passed away.",
