   "content": "<p>Amir Samh bin Malik Khawlani</p><p>718 CE to 721 CE</p><p>Hazrat &#x27;Umar bin Abd al-Aziz, while appointing Amir Samh bin Khawlani amir, instructed that a detailed review of the conditions of Andalus be taken; that un-Islamic laws and unlawful taxes be ended immediately; and that if the Muslims in Andalus are distressed and there is no prospect of improvement in the future, they should come back at once. Khawlani reached Andalus in April 718 CE. He reviewed all the laws and taxes carefully. Un-Islamic laws and taxes were immediately abrogated.</p><p>In the other taxes the share of the centre was fixed according to Islamic laws. Amir Khawlani also reviewed the overall conditions of Andalus. The conditions of the Muslims were learnt especially. He reached this conclusion that it is necessary for the Muslims to remain in Andalus. So he informed Hazrat &#x27;Umar bin Abd al-Aziz too of this situation. With the death of Hazrat &#x27;Umar bin Abd al-Aziz the royal era began again. For this reason Amir Khawlani stopped giving taxes and kharaj to the centre, and with this, plans were begun for the betterment of the public of Andalus. Near Cordoba the bridge of Wadi al-Kabir had become old. This bridge was rebuilt. The Jami&#x27; Mosque of Saragossa was built.</p>",
