     "text": "Abd al-Rahman al-Dakhil got very little leisure in life. Continuous struggle was in his destiny. In his era the wall of Cordoba had become useless. He had it repaired so that the city would remain safe from enemies. The palace of the ancient emperor was made the government palace, and changes in it changed it completely. Abd al-Rahman al-Dakhil had a beautiful palace built in Cordoba. He named it Qasr al-Rusafah after the name of the palace built by his grandfather Hisham. In it plants were brought from outside and planted. Water was brought to the city by means of pipes. A Jami' Mosque was built; 80 thousand dinars were spent on it. Seeing its beautiful minaret Abd al-Rahman used to say: \"This mosque wants a caliph; I am only an amir.\"",
