     "text": "Abd al-Rahman II had popularity among the public. In him were present all those qualities which are necessary for a ruler. Abd al-Rahman continued to receive the cooperation of his brothers; only Abdullah revolted, but hearing of the setting out of a unit of Abd al-Rahman's army he fled towards Valencia, and died in 823 CE. The flames of rivalry between the Mudari and Yamani tribes flared up again. To extinguish this fire Abd al-Rahman offered Abu al-Shammakh Mudari a high post in the army. Instead of Tudmir, Murcia was made the capital. Peace was restored in Merida and Toledo.",
