     "text": "… began plunder. Yusuf thought that the rulers of the small states of Andalus would join together in jihad. But Amir Ibn Abi Bakr informed Yusuf of the opposing ideas of these rulers and of the real conditions. Yusuf wrote: tell the rulers of these states to join you in jihad; if they do not agree, take possession of their regions. The jurists of the Ummah too gave the fatwa that it is permissible for Yusuf to depose these rulers and take possession of their wealth. So first of all Yusuf turned towards Granada, and the ruler of Granada, Abdullah, was arrested. Mu'tamid, the ruler of Seville, was sent to Africa in 1095 CE. Mu'tamid died right there. The Muslims took possession of Valencia. Yusuf took possession of vast regions from Tunis to the coast of the Atlantic Ocean.",
