     "text": "Yahya bin Laythi belonged to the Masmudah tribe. This was a Berber tribe. First of all he performed Hajj. In 795 CE he became a pupil of Hazrat Imam Malik. He received the teaching of the Muwatta'. In Egypt he learned sciences from Layth Ibn Sa'd and in Makkah al-Mu'azzamah from Sufyan Ibn 'Uyaynah. He was of a high degree of piety and righteousness. In the era of government of Abd al-Rahman he announced the decisions of criminal cases. He was very outspoken and fearless. In justice and fairness [he made no distinction between] rich and poor, amirs, viziers — even if it were against the caliph himself. Yahya wanted to obtain not the pleasure of the king but the pleasure of Allah Almighty. In Abd al-Rahman's court Yahya had a high place. Abd al-Rahman, while recruiting qadis, certainly consulted Yahya. According to Ibn Hazm, in the East Hanafi fiqh obtained the support of the king because of Imam Abu Hanifah and Qadi Abu Yusuf, and in the West Maliki fiqh because of Yahya. He died in 849 CE.",
