   "content": "<p>Chapter: 10</p><p>Islamic Spain … on the highway of progress</p><p>What did the Muslims give Europe? What did they get from Europe?</p><p>The Muslims entered Andalus as saviours. At the invitation of the oppressed of Andalus the Muslims turned towards Andalus. They became protectors of the poor. When the Muslims entered Europe, at that time Europe was drowned in the darkness of ignorance. The feudal system had made the life of the public difficult. Nothing of the peasants, cultivators and labourers was safe. Life, property and honour were at the mercy of landlords and jagirdars. Their wives and children too were considered the property of the jagirdars. Without the consent of the merciless masters even breathing was difficult for them. In respect of learning and civilisation Baghdad was at its height. Compared with it Europe was very far behind. In the whole of Europe no city of Baghdad&#x27;s standard existed. Through Andalus the scholarly treasure of Baghdad was transferred to Europe, and Europe, making it the foundation, advanced its sciences and arts and obtained its present progress. If today the scholarly and scientific progress of Europe is analysed, we reach this conclusion that in this progress the blood and sweat of the Muslims too is included.</p><p>1. Social progress:</p><p>In national progress social progress has a basic position. In Islamic Spain the Muslims …</p>",
